From: zonglvye <zonglvye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:41:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 76/90] feat(panel): dock the panel tabs at its bottom edge,
 like upstream v0.7.22

Replaces the icon-only strip at the top with the dock upstream's TabDock has:
it sits on the panel's bottom edge, shows every tab's name while the names fit
(measured by laying them out once out of sight), and falls back to icons for the
tabs that are not open when they do not. The raised mark under the chosen tab
slides across with framer-motion's layout animation.

The panel itself no longer scrolls - only the content between the header and the
dock does - and the card moves up 16px so the close handle stops covering the
last tab.
